#
# §188
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMadregaKeNegedSefirotOrotPartzufim a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Correspondence of each degree's parts to sefirot, lights and partzufim"@en, "Zuordnung der Teile jeder Stufe zu Sefirot, Lichtern, Parzufim"@de ;
    skos:definition "The head of each degree corresponds to Keter, yehida, Galgalta; its Atzilut (mouth to chest) to Hokhma, haya, AB; its Beria (chest to navel) to Bina, neshama, SaG; its Yetzira-Assiya (below navel) to ZON, ruah-nefesh, MaH and BoN."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Yehuda Leib Ashlag, in the Petiḥa le-Ḥokhmat ha-Qabbala" ;
    dcterms:date "1945"^^xsd:gYear ;
    skos:note "The ordering is the author's: he arranges the Lurianic material he expounds; the date is that of the printing read."@en ;
    skos:note "A correspondence between the parts of each degree, the sefirot, the lights and the partzufim; entered as an ordering."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:compilerInference ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:PetihaLeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Petiḥa le-Ḥokhmat ha-Qabbala, §188, Hebrew text of the Jerusalem 1945 printing with the Sulam commentary on the Zohar as given in the Sefaria library (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer); translations compared: Bnei Baruch; Steinhart 2023 covers §1-45 only" .

